.TH KOSH 5 "2026-08-04" "kosh" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
kosh \- shell startup configuration files
.SH DESCRIPTION
The startup configuration files contain shell commands. The startup chain
selects each file for a mood. The file is parsed with that mood's grammar. There
is no separate syntax for sections, directives, keys, or values.
.PP
Commands, comments, quoting, expansion, redirection, functions, and builtins use
the syntax defined by
.BR kosh (1).
See
.BR kosh (1)
for startup discovery, loading order, suppression, and error handling.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/koshrc
This is the system configuration file for an interactive
.B kosh
mood.
.TP
.I ~/.koshrc
This is the user configuration file for an interactive
.B kosh
mood.
.TP
.I /etc/profile
This is the system login configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.profile
This is the user POSIX login configuration file and the last Bash login
candidate.
.TP
.I ~/.bash_profile
This is the first user Bash login candidate.
.TP
.I ~/.bash_login
This is the second user Bash login candidate.
.TP
.IR /etc/bash/bashrc " or " /etc/bash.bashrc
The first readable path is the system configuration file for an interactive
non-login Bash mood.
.TP
.I ~/.bashrc
This is the default user configuration file for an interactive non-login Bash
mood.
.TP
.I /usr/share/bash-completion/bash_completion
This file supplies Bash programmable completion after the Bash startup chain
sources an rc file. It is skipped when completion is disabled, when a default
completion specification exists, and when BASH_COMPLETION_VERSINFO is already
set.
.PP
The
.B \-\-rcfile
and
.B \-\-init\-file
options and the ENV and BASH_ENV variables may select a different file. See
.BR kosh (1)
for their conditions and expansion rules.
.SH SYNTAX
LF and CRLF terminate a line. A CRLF pair is one newline. A lone carriage return
remains source text.
.PP
A number sign begins a shell comment where the shell lexical rules recognize a
comment. Assignments, shell options, functions, aliases, and commands take
effect in the shell that sources the file. A sourced configuration file may
select a runtime mood with
.B set \-\-mood
or request another startup chain with
.BR "set \-\-init\-moods" .
A mood whose files are already being sourced is not reentered.
.SH ERRORS
A missing optional file, custom rc file, or BASH_ENV file is skipped. An
existing custom rc or BASH_ENV file is skipped with a diagnostic if it cannot
be read. An unreadable ENV file is skipped without a diagnostic. Syntax and
execution errors produce the ordinary shell diagnostics described in
.BR kosh (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kosh (1)
